1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,738
Support can be expensive.

2
00:00:01,738 --> 00:00:04,429
And sharing personal concerns with a room

3
00:00:04,429 --> 00:00:06,735
full of strangers can feel difficult.

4
00:00:06,735 --> 00:00:11,348
Meet Irene: a private first step toward affordable, therapist led group support.

5
00:00:12,167 --> 00:00:13,538
The idea is simple.

6
00:00:13,538 --> 00:00:17,653
One therapist leads a suitable group, and the session fee is shared.

7
00:00:17,653 --> 00:00:20,738
For example, a twenty four hundred rupee session split

8
00:00:20,738 --> 00:00:23,481
between six people is four hundred rupees each.

9
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:26,910
Actual fees and group sizes are set by the therapist.

10
00:00:27,733 --> 00:00:30,854
Here is the live app, using a fictional participant.

11
00:00:30,854 --> 00:00:34,321
The person chooses a program and begins a private intake.

12
00:00:34,321 --> 00:00:36,402
Other participants cannot read their story.

13
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:41,375
They set their availability, sharing comfort, and maximum session budget.

14
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:45,103
These practical constraints matter alongside shared concerns, so a

15
00:00:45,103 --> 00:00:48,830
promising match also needs to work in everyday life.

16
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:53,399
With explicit consent, the participant describes their concerns and goals.

17
00:00:53,399 --> 00:00:56,788
In this example, a fictional student wants more confidence

18
00:00:56,788 --> 00:01:00,178
speaking in class and a stronger sense of connection.

19
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,456
Gemini turns that intake into a draft summary and structured matching features.

20
00:01:05,456 --> 00:01:08,056
The participant can correct the summary before

21
00:01:08,056 --> 00:01:10,284
confirming it for their chosen therapist.

22
00:01:10,284 --> 00:01:13,997
Possible risk or uncertainty signals are routed for human review.

23
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,756
Next, a verified therapist reviews the confirmed intake.

24
00:01:17,756 --> 00:01:20,713
They decide whether the person should be considered

25
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:23,670
for a group or needs an individual conversation.

26
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:26,626
AI does not diagnose or replace that judgment.

27
00:01:27,433 --> 00:01:31,491
Google embeddings help compare the meaning of concerns and goals.

28
00:01:31,491 --> 00:01:35,548
Irene combines similarity with practical constraints to suggest a circle.

29
00:01:35,548 --> 00:01:40,417
The therapist reviews the proposal, sets the session details, and approves invitations.

30
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:43,860
The participant sees the session and exact

31
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:46,112
individual quote, then accepts or declines.

32
00:01:46,112 --> 00:01:47,988
This demo collects no payment.

33
00:01:47,988 --> 00:01:50,615
The therapist can also generate a private

34
00:01:50,615 --> 00:01:52,867
AI preparation brief for the group.

35
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:57,392
Participants can review, export, or delete their intake data.

36
00:01:57,392 --> 00:02:00,674
Access is restricted by account role and assignment.

37
00:02:00,674 --> 00:02:03,545
The demonstration uses fictional information, and is

38
00:02:03,545 --> 00:02:06,006
not a clinical or emergency service.

39
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:10,629
Irene is live on Firebase Hosting and Google Cloud

40
00:02:10,629 --> 00:02:14,002
Run, with Gemini, Secret Manager, and Supabase PostgreSQL.

41
00:02:14,002 --> 00:02:18,220
Thirty backend tests and thirty five live workflow checks passed.

42
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,750
Clinical validation remains a next step.

43
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:24,085
Irene makes the first step private, the

44
00:02:24,085 --> 00:02:26,603
grouping thoughtful, and the session cost shared.

45
00:02:26,603 --> 00:02:28,042
A little less alone.

46
00:02:28,042 --> 00:02:29,481
Explore the live prototype.
